target:    tests/oracle/classify.py
gate:      composer test:classifier-plants
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    no rule claims the oracle BACKED an arm
rationale: Stops Facts.agrees() refusing a vacuous both-hollow agreement, which is how S4 shipped and
           is the MECHANISM the -02 entry is one instance of. Four rules read agrees() as evidence that
           the oracle backs an arm and only one had asked whether the oracle answered at all, so the
           hole was live in three: (a)/PASS through new-backed-registered, and - still live after that
           cell was patched - a manufactured release-blocking (b) through old-backed. The worst shape
           is old=empty new=zero oracle=empty: a surface that stopped returning no rows and started
           reporting a measured 0, which is a FIX, reported as 'the oracle backs OLD: a release-
           blocking regression' on the strength of an oracle that returned nothing. Measured: this
           restores 4 red assertions in section 4b, all of them the BACKED_BY_ORACLE clause, and moves
           7 triples off c-THREE-WAY. Fixed in agrees() and NOT in algebra: making both-hollow
           INCOMPARABLE turns one assertion red whose own mislabelling_means declares both-hollow EQUAL
           a load-bearing contract with a named owner.
---
diff --git a/tests/oracle/classify.py b/tests/oracle/classify.py
--- a/tests/oracle/classify.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/classify.py
@@ -270,7 +270,7 @@ class Facts:
         Between the two ARMS it is not — there the order came from two SQL engines and is a
         finding of its own, which is why ORDER-ONLY is a label and not a footnote.
         """
-        if algebra.rule_family(diff.rule) == "both-hollow":
+        if False:
             # Two empties compare EQUAL and always will (PITFALLS 38). On the ARMS leg that
             # is caught by `hollow-arms` before any value rule; on an ORACLE leg nothing
             # caught it, so an oracle that returned NOTHING was cited as backing an arm —
